Literature Review 2: Directed-Energy
Defense Scheduling
Extension of Literature Review 1. Prepared 6 November 2026 for Research Project 2.
Updated 7 November 2026.
1. Scope, method and limits
This document records the literature extension agreed after Literature Review 1:
snowballing from the related-work sections of Zhang 2026 and Li 2026, targeted searches
on classical weapon-target assignment (WTA), partial observability, stochastic scheduling
and the evaluation of learning against heuristics, and a check of the cluster-based WTA
paper by Sung et al.
Provenance tags. [DOC]: stated in a document I read for this review (extent in Section 2).
[REF]: known only from a search snippet, an abstract or another paper's reference list;
the cited work itself was not read. [MEM]: from my memory, unverified. [OPEN]:
unverified, or my own inference. Where a number was recomputed, the inputs are named.
Limits. Across the steps of 6 and 7 November I ran 25 web searches and 7 successful page
fetches. One fetch (ResearchGate, for Sung et al.) was blocked; Sung et al. was later read
from the project file. The publisher full text of Kracman 2025 is restricted and no open
copy was found. No bibliographic database (Scopus, Web of Science, IEEE Xplore search,
Google Scholar) was queried, so this is not a systematic search. Chinese-language work
was seen only through English abstracts.
