A laser fire-control patent, US 4,647,759 (snippet): states that dwell time, slew time
and fuel limits must be considered in laser fire control. It shows the scheduling
problem was recognised outside the academic literature long ago. Claims not verified;
patents are not used as evidence of novelty.
A Defence Science Review item on laser directed-energy weapons (2025 per snippet;
title and authors not captured): says classical WTA frameworks do not fully reflect
laser characteristics.
One more search on laser engagement scheduling with dwell, deadlines and slew
found no directed-energy paper with stochastic dwell, unknown hardness and
learned-policy comparison [OPEN; not exhaustive].
