6. Go or no-go
6.1 G5: go, narrowed
Safe wording for the paper: none of the DE-specific RL schedulers we reviewed compares
against a dynamic optimization baseline. Do not write that no RLWTA paper compares
with optimization. Baselines to implement: fair allocation; difficulty-aware greedy
(marginal return); a receding-horizon optimizer over sampled scenarios; MILP or crossentropy at small scale.
6.2 G8 (Option D): conditional go for a bounded pilot, not yet the anchor of the
paper
For: no DE-specific work on probing and abandonment with accumulating dwell found;
Chen's results do not transfer directly because shots are memoryless; the robustness
result for Gittins policies gives a reason to expect prior misspecification to matter.
Against: the search was not systematic; kills-by-deadline objectives are generally
outside Gittins optimality [MEM, unverified]; the theory may be intractable beyond
toy cases; the bandit-shooting lineage (Glazebrook et al.) already covers learning
target type from failed shots and optimal disengagement for memoryless shots, so a
novelty claim must rest on deadlines, slew and dwell accumulation.
Test: pilot P0 in Section 8.
